; 🔴 It differs from StageCard by its border's WIDTH as well as its hue, and the width is not a
; flourish: the warning that the hero is under the stage's recommendation is status information, and
; this project's rule is that status is never carried by colour alone. Ember against the card's
; grey-violet edge is a hue swap and very little else — the two edges are 0.41 and 0.24 relative
; luminance, so a player who cannot separate the hues is reading a 1.7:1 difference on an 8-unit
; line. A 24-unit rule down the leading edge is a shape, and it reads on any palette.
;
; Left edge only, because the card is 156 tall and holds a 144 tap target: a heavier top or bottom
; border would draw over the Change control. The left content margin is 33, so a 24 border sits
; inside padding the card already spends.
[sub_resource type="StyleBoxFlat" id="StyleBoxFlat_stage_card_warned"]
